### Create a transaction (IntelliJ HTTP Client). Re-run this request: the second call is replayed.
### X-Correlation-Id is optional; it is echoed back and appears in every related log line.
POST http://localhost:8080/transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: tx-demo-0001
X-Correlation-Id: demo-trace-001

{
  "accountId": "acc-1",
  "amount": 100.50,
  "currency": "EUR",
  "reference": "order-42"
}

> {% client.global.set("txId", response.body.id); %}

### Same key, different payload -> 422
POST http://localhost:8080/transactions
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: tx-demo-0001

{
  "accountId": "acc-1",
  "amount": 999,
  "currency": "EUR"
}

### Approve the transaction created above (202; re-run: replayed, not recorded twice)
POST http://localhost:8080/events
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ev-demo-0000

{
  "transactionId": "{{txId}}",
  "type": "APPROVED",
  "payload": {"authCode": "A1B2"}
}

### Submit (expected after approval)
POST http://localhost:8080/events
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ev-demo-0001

{ "transactionId": "{{txId}}", "type": "SUBMITTED" }

### Reserve
POST http://localhost:8080/events
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ev-demo-0002

{ "transactionId": "{{txId}}", "type": "RESERVED" }

### Settle
POST http://localhost:8080/events
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ev-demo-0003

{ "transactionId": "{{txId}}", "type": "SETTLED" }

### Reverse (terminal)
POST http://localhost:8080/events
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ev-demo-0004

{ "transactionId": "{{txId}}", "type": "REVERSED" }

### Duplicate APPROVED with a new key: accepted, shows up in reconciliation
POST http://localhost:8080/events
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: ev-demo-0005

{ "transactionId": "{{txId}}", "type": "APPROVED" }

### Reconciliation report, now
GET http://localhost:8080/reconciliation/report

### Reconciliation report as if 3 minutes had passed
< {%
  const later = new Date(Date.now() + 3 * 60 * 1000).toISOString();
  request.variables.set("later", later);
%}
GET http://localhost:8080/reconciliation/report?asOf={{later}}

### Read the transaction read model back (updated asynchronously by the consumer)
GET http://localhost:8080/transactions/{{txId}}

### Event stream, in receive order
GET http://localhost:8080/transactions/{{txId}}/events

### Rebuild the read model by replaying the stream
POST http://localhost:8080/transactions/{{txId}}/replay

### Dead-lettered events (events the consumer could not apply)
GET http://localhost:8080/dead-letters

### Health
GET http://localhost:8080/actuator/health
